    <section class="slide" data-title="Sample adequacy" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Sampling logic</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>What makes a sample size “good”?</h2>
          <div class="sample-adequacy-definition">
            <p><strong>A good sample size is adequate for the intended claim.</strong> Quantitative adequacy means enough precision or power under stated assumptions. Qualitative adequacy means enough information-rich evidence for the design and analytic purpose.</p>
            <div class="adequacy-criteria" aria-label="Four tests of sample adequacy"><span><b>Claim fit</b>Who or what will the result describe?</span><span><b>Design fit</b>What comparison, estimate or interpretation is planned?</span><span><b>Uncertainty</b>How much error, variation or analytic depth matters?</span><span><b>Transparency</b>Which assumptions and stopping rules will be reported?</span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="sample-size-intro">Common practices offer planning anchors. Select a route, inspect the cited recommendations, then justify how the final target fits the present study.</p>
          <div class="sample-size-workbench" data-sample-size-explorer>
            <nav class="sample-size-routes" aria-label="Choose a sample size practice">
              <button type="button" data-sample-size-route="quantitative" aria-controls="sample-size-en-quantitative" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Quantitative</strong><span>Power benchmarks</span></button>
              <button type="button" data-sample-size-route="qualitative" aria-controls="sample-size-en-qualitative" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Qualitative</strong><span>Design suggestions</span></button>
              <button type="button" data-sample-size-route="focus-groups" aria-controls="sample-size-en-focus-groups" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Focus groups</strong><span>People per group</span></button>
              <button type="button" data-sample-size-route="adjustments" aria-controls="sample-size-en-adjustments" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Adjustments</strong><span>From base n to recruitment</span></button>
            </nav>
            <div class="sample-size-stage" aria-live="polite">
              <div class="sample-size-empty" data-sample-size-empty><strong>Start with the study’s claim</strong><p>Choose the practice closest to the intended design. Treat each number as a conditional planning anchor.</p></div>
              <article id="sample-size-en-quantitative" class="sample-size-panel" data-sample-size-panel="quantitative" hidden>
                <header><span>Published planning benchmarks</span><h3>Quantitative designs</h3></header>
                <div class="recommendation-grid recommendation-grid--three">
                  <p><b>Correlational</b><strong>64</strong> for a one-tailed hypothesis; <strong>82</strong> for a two-tailed hypothesis.<cite>Onwuegbuzie et al., 2004</cite></p>
                  <p><b>Causal-comparative</b><strong>51 per group</strong> for one-tailed; <strong>64 per group</strong> for two-tailed.<cite>Onwuegbuzie et al., 2004</cite></p>
                  <p><b>Experimental</b><strong>21 per group</strong> for a one-tailed hypothesis.<cite>Onwuegbuzie et al., 2004</cite></p>
                </div>
                <p class="sample-size-caution">These benchmarks assume a medium effect, .80 power and α = .05. Tail direction, expected effect, variance, allocation and analysis can change the required sample.</p>
              </article>
              <article id="sample-size-en-qualitative" class="sample-size-panel" data-sample-size-panel="qualitative" hidden>
                <header><span>Published design suggestions</span><h3>Qualitative designs</h3></header>
                <div class="recommendation-grid recommendation-grid--five">
                  <p><b>Case study</b><strong>3–5 participants</strong><cite>Creswell, 2002</cite></p>
                  <p><b>Phenomenology</b><strong>≤10 interviews; ≥6 participants</strong><cite>Creswell, 1998; Morse, 1994</cite></p>
                  <p><b>Grounded theory</b><strong>15–20 or 20–30</strong><cite>Creswell, 2002; Creswell, 1998</cite></p>
                  <p><b>Ethnography</b><strong>1 cultural group; 30–50 interviews</strong><cite>Creswell, 2002; Morse, 1994</cite></p>
                  <p><b>Ethological study</b><strong>100–200 observation units</strong><cite>Morse, 1994</cite></p>
                </div>
                <p class="sample-size-caution">Use these as design-specific starting points. Information richness, participant specificity, variation and analytic depth determine adequacy; define and document saturation when it is an appropriate stopping criterion.</p>
              </article>
              <article id="sample-size-en-focus-groups" class="sample-size-panel" data-sample-size-panel="focus-groups" hidden>
                <header><span>Method-level suggestions</span><h3>Participants in each focus group</h3></header>
                <div class="focus-group-ranges">
                  <p><strong>6–9</strong><cite>Krueger, 2000</cite></p>
                  <p><strong>6–10</strong><cite>Langford et al., 2002; Morgan, 1997</cite></p>
                  <p><strong>6–12</strong><cite>Johnson &amp; Christensen, 2004; Bernard, 1995</cite></p>
                  <p><strong>8–12</strong><cite>Baumgartner et al., 2002</cite></p>
                </div>
                <div class="formula-band formula-band-text"><strong>Group size and number of groups answer different planning questions</strong><small>Plan enough interaction within each group and enough groups to cover relevant variation.</small></div>
                <p class="sample-size-caution">Report how participants were composed across groups and how the stopping decision was reached.</p>
              </article>
              <article id="sample-size-en-adjustments" class="sample-size-panel" data-sample-size-panel="adjustments" hidden>
                <header><span>From planning to fieldwork</span><h3>Adjust the initial target for the way the study will run</h3></header>
                <div class="sample-size-sequence" aria-label="Sample size adjustment sequence"><span>Claim</span><b>→</b><span>Base n</span><b>→</b><span>Design effect</span><b>→</b><span>Attrition</span><b>→</b><span>Recruit</span></div>
                <div class="sample-size-notes"><p><b>Clustering</b>Increase the target when participants share classrooms, schools or sites because members of the same group may respond similarly.</p><p><b>Nonresponse or attrition</b>Recruit above the number of complete cases needed. For example, retaining 278 participants with 85% expected retention requires a target of about 328 recruits.</p></div>
                <p class="sample-size-caution">The base n is the sample required under the initial statistical model before clustering, attrition, unequal allocation or other design adjustments.</p>
              </article>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="sample-size-source">Recommendations compiled in <a href="https://doi.org/10.2167/eri421.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Collins, Onwuegbuzie, and Jiao (2006), Table 2</a>. They are planning references whose assumptions should be checked for the present study.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>甚麼令樣本量稱得上「良好」？</h2>
          <div class="sample-adequacy-definition">
            <p><strong>良好樣本量足以支持預期主張。</strong>量化研究需要在清楚假設下提供足夠精確度或統計功效；質性研究則需要與設計及分析目的相稱的資訊豐富證據。</p>
            <div class="adequacy-criteria" aria-label="樣本充分性的四項檢驗"><span><b>主張切合度</b>結果將描述誰或甚麼？</span><span><b>設計切合度</b>計劃作出哪種比較、估計或詮釋？</span><span><b>不確定性</b>多少誤差、變異或分析深度才重要？</span><span><b>透明度</b>將報告哪些假設及停止準則？</span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="sample-size-intro">常見做法提供規劃錨點。選擇一條路徑，閱讀附有引文的建議，再說明最終目標如何切合當前研究。</p>
          <div class="sample-size-workbench" data-sample-size-explorer>
            <nav class="sample-size-routes" aria-label="選擇一項樣本量做法">
              <button type="button" data-sample-size-route="quantitative" aria-controls="sample-size-zh-quantitative" aria-pressed="false"><strong>量化研究</strong><span>統計功效基準</span></button>
              <button type="button" data-sample-size-route="qualitative" aria-controls="sample-size-zh-qualitative" aria-pressed="false"><strong>質性研究</strong><span>設計建議</span></button>
              <button type="button" data-sample-size-route="focus-groups" aria-controls="sample-size-zh-focus-groups" aria-pressed="false"><strong>焦點小組</strong><span>每組人數</span></button>
              <button type="button" data-sample-size-route="adjustments" aria-controls="sample-size-zh-adjustments" aria-pressed="false"><strong>調整</strong><span>由基礎 n 至招募</span></button>
            </nav>
            <div class="sample-size-stage" aria-live="polite">
              <div class="sample-size-empty" data-sample-size-empty><strong>先由研究主張出發</strong><p>選擇最接近預期設計的做法，並把每個數字視為有條件的規劃錨點。</p></div>
              <article id="sample-size-zh-quantitative" class="sample-size-panel" data-sample-size-panel="quantitative" hidden>
                <header><span>已發表的規劃基準</span><h3>量化研究設計</h3></header>
                <div class="recommendation-grid recommendation-grid--three">
                  <p><b>相關研究</b>單尾假設 <strong>64 人</strong>；雙尾假設 <strong>82 人</strong>。<cite>Onwuegbuzie et al., 2004</cite></p>
                  <p><b>因果比較研究</b>單尾每組 <strong>51 人</strong>；雙尾每組 <strong>64 人</strong>。<cite>Onwuegbuzie et al., 2004</cite></p>
                  <p><b>實驗研究</b>單尾假設每組 <strong>21 人</strong>。<cite>Onwuegbuzie et al., 2004</cite></p>
                </div>
                <p class="sample-size-caution">這些基準假設中等效果、.80 統計功效及 α = .05。尾向、預期效果、變異、分配及分析方法都可能改變所需樣本。</p>
              </article>
              <article id="sample-size-zh-qualitative" class="sample-size-panel" data-sample-size-panel="qualitative" hidden>
                <header><span>已發表的設計建議</span><h3>質性研究設計</h3></header>
                <div class="recommendation-grid recommendation-grid--five">
                  <p><b>個案研究</b><strong>3–5 名參與者</strong><cite>Creswell, 2002</cite></p>
                  <p><b>現象學</b><strong>≤10 次訪談；≥6 名參與者</strong><cite>Creswell, 1998; Morse, 1994</cite></p>
                  <p><b>紮根理論</b><strong>15–20 或 20–30 人</strong><cite>Creswell, 2002; Creswell, 1998</cite></p>
                  <p><b>民族誌</b><strong>1 個文化群體；30–50 次訪談</strong><cite>Creswell, 2002; Morse, 1994</cite></p>
                  <p><b>行為觀察研究</b><strong>100–200 個觀察單位</strong><cite>Morse, 1994</cite></p>
                </div>
                <p class="sample-size-caution">把這些數字視為設計特定的起點。資訊豐富度、參與者特定性、所需差異及分析深度共同決定充分性；若飽和適合作為停止準則，應先界定並記錄它。</p>
              </article>
              <article id="sample-size-zh-focus-groups" class="sample-size-panel" data-sample-size-panel="focus-groups" hidden>
                <header><span>研究方法層面的建議</span><h3>每個焦點小組的參與者人數</h3></header>
                <div class="focus-group-ranges">
                  <p><strong>6–9 人</strong><cite>Krueger, 2000</cite></p>
                  <p><strong>6–10 人</strong><cite>Langford et al., 2002; Morgan, 1997</cite></p>
                  <p><strong>6–12 人</strong><cite>Johnson &amp; Christensen, 2004; Bernard, 1995</cite></p>
                  <p><strong>8–12 人</strong><cite>Baumgartner et al., 2002</cite></p>
                </div>
                <div class="formula-band formula-band-text"><strong>每組人數與小組數量是兩項不同的規劃問題</strong><small>每組需要足夠互動，也需要足夠小組涵蓋相關差異。</small></div>
                <p class="sample-size-caution">報告各組參與者的組成方式，以及如何作出停止收集資料的決定。</p>
              </article>
              <article id="sample-size-zh-adjustments" class="sample-size-panel" data-sample-size-panel="adjustments" hidden>
                <header><span>由規劃走向田野</span><h3>按照研究實際進行方式調整初始目標</h3></header>
                <div class="sample-size-sequence" aria-label="樣本量調整流程"><span>主張</span><b>→</b><span>基礎 n</span><b>→</b><span>設計效應</span><b>→</b><span>流失</span><b>→</b><span>招募</span></div>
                <div class="sample-size-notes"><p><b>叢集</b>參與者同屬班級、學校或場域時，組內成員可能較相似，因此應提高目標樣本量。</p><p><b>無回應或流失</b>招募人數應高於所需完整個案數。例如，預期留存率為 85%，若要保留 278 名參與者，招募目標約為 328 人。</p></div>
                <p class="sample-size-caution">基礎 n 指初始統計模型要求的樣本量，尚未計入叢集、流失、不等比例分配或其他設計調整。</p>
              </article>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="sample-size-source">建議彙整自 <a href="https://doi.org/10.2167/eri421.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Collins、Onwuegbuzie 與 Jiao（2006），表 2</a>。這些數字是規劃參考，使用時應檢查它們的假設是否適用於當前研究。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Evidence to claim" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Research quality</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Quality asks whether the inference is warranted</h2>
          <div class="path-line quality-chain">
            <span>Question</span><b>→</b><span>Evidence</span><b>→</b><span>Analysis</span><b>→</b><span>Claim</span>
          </div>
          <div class="grid-3 quality-questions">
            <article class="panel"><h3>Accuracy</h3><p>Does the evidence represent the intended construct, experience or process?</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Alternatives</h3><p>Could bias, confounding, selection or interpretation produce another account?</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Boundary</h3><p>How far beyond these participants, cases, conditions and measures may the claim travel?</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>研究品質關乎推論是否有充分理據</h2>
          <div class="path-line quality-chain">
            <span>研究問題</span><b>→</b><span>證據</span><b>→</b><span>分析</span><b>→</b><span>主張</span>
          </div>
          <div class="grid-3 quality-questions">
